course: dictionary
lesson: 7827
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «Her lip quivered.» Here quiver means to shake slightly and quickly, because a lip cannot carry arrows.
explain: Read the words around the word. «The Mole's nose quivers… a quick run, a stop, a try back, then a sure advance.» The nose is moving in small, quick shakes, so quivers means shakes slightly and quickly.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In a story, a quivering voice often shows fear, cold or strong feeling. In history, a quiver is a case for arrows. If your meaning fits the sentence, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Quiver can be a verb or a noun, so check how it is used in the sentence.
fact: As a verb, «quiver» means to shake slightly and quickly.
fact: As a noun, «a quiver» means a slight trembling movement or sound, or a case for carrying arrows.
fact: In stories, «quivering» often shows fear, cold or strong feeling, such as a quivering lip before crying.
fact: Archers such as Robin Hood carried their arrows in a quiver, worn on the back or hip.
exercise: «Her lip quivered before she began to cry.» What does quivered mean? | *Shook slightly and quickly | Sang loudly | Smiled widely | Fell fast asleep
exercise: Robin Hood pulled an arrow from his quiver. What is a quiver? | A bow made of wood | Sleeping bag for the forest | *A case for carrying arrows | A small grey bird
exercise: «In science, a plucked string quivers to make sound.» What does quivers mean here? | Stays perfectly still | *Trembles with a quick, small movement | Breaks into pieces | Sings a happy tune
test: «Her voice quivered with fear as she spoke.» What does quivered suggest? | She was bouncing with joy | *She was frightened or upset | She was bored and tired | She was very hungry
test: Ben says, «I saw a quiver of light on the water.» Which meaning fits best? | *A slight trembling movement | A heavy wave crashing | A case for arrows | A loud and sudden bang
exam: «The Mole's nose quivers, a quick run, a stop, a try back.» Which meaning of quivers fits best? | Stays still and silent | A case for carrying arrows | *Shakes slightly and quickly | Falls heavily to the ground
